# 25. Why Shared Funding May Be More Efficient

Wildfires do not respect insurance-company boundaries.

A fire prevented near one property may protect hundreds of neighboring properties insured by different companies.

Therefore:

**wildfire prevention has a shared-benefit problem.**

If only one insurer pays for prevention, other insurers may benefit without contributing.

A shared regional funding mechanism could reduce this free-rider problem.

---

# 26. Governance and Data Separation

Insurance companies may help fund the system, but they should not automatically control operational surveillance data.

A safer governance structure is:

**Insurance companies fund.**

**Fire authorities command.**

**Independent infrastructure stores operational data.**

**Community hosts provide physical locations.**

This prevents financial stakeholders from gaining inappropriate access to private surveillance data.

